# Validation
## Rubric
- [x] Confirm the changed matcher slices policy-controlled UTF-8 using a byte index from `prefix.len()` after only a byte-length check.
- [x] Identify an actual prefix resolver whose ASCII prefix length can be targeted; first prefix is `s3:ExistingObjectTag/` with length 21.
- [x] Construct a valid JSON bucket policy whose condition key length is >= 21 and whose byte offset 21 is not a UTF-8 character boundary.
- [x] Exercise the real parse and validation path (`parse_bucket_policy` then `validate_evaluable_object_conditions`) rather than a standalone copy of the matcher.
- [x] Produce direct crash evidence and attempt secondary validation with debugger/valgrind; LLDB confirmed the vulnerable frame and valgrind was unavailable.
## Report
Validated the suspected panic with a targeted Rust integration-test PoC. Code review of the touched path shows `KeyMatch::match_key` checks only `key.len() >= prefix.len()` and then calls `key.split_at(prefix.len())` at `crates/auth/src/bucket_policy/condition_key.rs:74-75`. The condition-key table begins with the ASCII prefix `s3:ExistingObjectTag/` at `condition_key.rs:142`; its length is 21 bytes. Lookup iterates policy-supplied condition keys through `resolver.key.match_key(key)` at `condition_key.rs:431-433`, and policy validation reaches this via `clause_action_status()` at `condition_key.rs:793-797` from `BucketPolicy::validate_evaluable_object_conditions()` at `crates/auth/src/bucket_policy.rs:133-135` and `conditions_supported_for_policy_actions()` at `bucket_policy.rs:1027-1030`. The PutBucketPolicy path parses attacker-supplied JSON and then calls this validator at `crates/server-core/src/coordinator/authz/bucket.rs:536-549`.

The PoC test creates a valid JSON bucket policy with condition key `aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaé` where byte index 21 falls inside the two-byte UTF-8 `é`. Running `RUST_BACKTRACE=1 cargo test -p auth --test utf8_condition_panic -- --nocapture` exits 101 and panics: `end byte index 21 is not a char boundary; it is inside 'é' (bytes 20..22) of `aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaé``. The stack includes `core::str::<impl str>::split_at`, `auth::bucket_policy::condition_key::KeyMatch::match_key` at `condition_key.rs:75:53`, `lookup` at `condition_key.rs:433:43`, `clause_action_status` at `condition_key.rs:797:36`, and `BucketPolicy::validate_evaluable_object_conditions` at `bucket_policy.rs:135:27`.

Debugger validation was also attempted with LLDB. A breakpoint at `condition_key.rs:75` stopped with `key=(data_ptr = "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaé", length = 22)` immediately before `split_at(prefix.len())`; the LLDB backtrace confirmed the same call chain from `validate_evaluable_object_conditions()` to `match_key()`. Valgrind was attempted but unavailable in the container (`bash: command not found: valgrind`).

